Rips_ClaimPrizes
├── when the round is not finalized
│   └── it should revert.
├── when recipient is zero address
│   └── it should revert.
├── when start index is out of bounds
│   └── it should revert.
├── when all ranges in scope are already claimed
│   └── it should not transfer any funds.
└── when there are unclaimed ranges
    ├── it should mark processed ranges as claimed.
    ├── it should calculate correct prizes using the affine permutation.
    ├── when recipient is different from the caller
    │   └── it should transfer the prize to the recipient, not the caller.
    ├── given the stake currency is native
    │   ├── when protocol fee is zero
    │   │   ├── it should transfer the full ETH prize to the recipient.
    │   │   └── it should emit a {PrizesClaimed} event.
    │   └── when protocol fee is greater than zero
    │       ├── it should transfer the fee in ETH to the fee recipient.
    │       ├── it should transfer the remaining ETH prize to the recipient.
    │       └── it should emit a {PrizesClaimed} event.
    └── given the stake currency is an ERC20 token
        ├── when protocol fee is zero
        │   ├── it should transfer the full token prize to the recipient.
        │   └── it should emit a {PrizesClaimed} event.
        └── when protocol fee is greater than zero
            ├── it should transfer the fee in tokens to the fee recipient.
            ├── it should transfer the remaining token prize to the recipient.
            └── it should emit a {PrizesClaimed} event.
